{
  "dom_id": "step-q342926",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find ${y}^{′}(0)$ when $y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}.$\n\n${y}^{′}(0)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2)}$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{u},\\,u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡v,\\,v=5x+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡v\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡v\\operatorname{cot}⁡v)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x+2))\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x+2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5x+2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${y}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5(0)+2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(5(0)+2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2)\\sqrt{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
